{
  "formatVersion": 1,
  "id": "x-touch-default-1",
  "name": "X-Touch Default 1",
  "notes": "Default X-Touch layout 1 (v1 mappings/xTouch1.json): faders on executors 201-208 + main 209, encoders on 401-408, button rows on 401-408 / 301-308 / 201-208 / 101-108, F-keys on 191-198, view row on 291-298, QuickKeys and MA commands on the master section. Converted from v1. The timecodeSelect button cycles through timecode slots 0-8 on every press (0 = none), exactly as in v1. Encoder push buttons carried executor feedback in v1 that the hardware ignored (no LED there) — represented here as feedback 'none'. Modifier buttons (encoder fine/rough, attribute select) keep 'on-off' feedback because v1 drove those LEDs locally (toggle state / selected attribute). Command buttons (Highlight/Solo/Blind/Freeze/...) use 'on-off' feedback: the engine lights them from the MA3 master state (/masterEnabled), exactly as in v1.",
  "deviceDefinitionId": "x-touch",
  "midiPort": {
    "input": "X-Touch",
    "output": "X-Touch"
  },
  "enableTimecodeSend": true,
